 <% layout("layout/boilerplate") %>
 
 <style>
    body {
      background: #f5f8f5;
      color: #26352b;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    .hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #124b2b, #269653);
      color: white;
      padding: 65px 20px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
      font-weight: 800;
    }

    .hero p {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 15px auto 0;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .section-heading {
      color: #176638;
      font-weight: 800;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .step-card, .feature-card, .info-panel {
      background: white;
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 25px;
      height: 100%;
      box-shadow: 0 5px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.06);
      border: 1px solid #e6eee7;
    }

    .step-number {
      background: #198754;
      color: white;
      border-radius: 50%;
      width: 44px;
      height: 44px;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: bold;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }

    .feature-icon {
      font-size: 35px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .step-card h4, .feature-card h4 {
      color: #185d35;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .step-card p, .feature-card p, .info-panel p {
      line-height: 1.75;
      color: #526057;
    }

    .notice {
      background: #e7f5eb;
      border-left: 5px solid #198754;
      padding: 20px;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }

    .footer {
      background: #124b2b;
      color: white;
      padding: 24px;
      text-align: center;
      margin-top: 50px;
    }

    .btn-explore {
      background: white;
      color: #176638;
      font-weight: bold;
      padding: 12px 25px;
      border-radius: 30px;
      text-decoration: none;
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 24px;
    }

    .btn-explore:hover {
      background: #e6f4e9;
      color: #124b2b;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>How Maharashtra Tourism Works</h1>

      <p>
        Your step-by-step guide to discovering beautiful destinations,
        planning your journey, organizing trips, and accessing tourist
        safety features across Maharashtra.
      </p>

      <a href="/explore" class="btn-explore">
        Start Exploring Maharashtra →
      </a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="container py-5">

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <section class="mb-5">
      <h2 class="section-heading">What Is This Platform?</h2>

      <p>
        Maharashtra Tourism is a digital tourism platform that brings
        destination discovery, trip planning, route assistance, and
        tourist safety tools together in one place. It is designed
        for people who want to explore Maharashtra's forts, temples,
        historical monuments, wildlife destinations, beaches, and
        natural attractions.
      </p>

      <p>
        Instead of collecting all your travel information from
        different places, you can use the application's available
        features to prepare and organize your journey.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Getting Started -->
    <section class="mb-5">
      <h2 class="section-heading">How to Use the Application</h2>

      <p class="text-secondary mb-4">
        Follow these steps to get started with your tourism journey.
      </p>

      <div class="row g-4">

        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-number">1</div>
            <h4>Create an Account</h4>
            <p>
              Sign up and log in if the feature you want requires an
              account. Your account allows you to access the
              application's login-protected features.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-number">2</div>
            <h4>Explore Destinations</h4>
            <p>
              Open the destination or Explore section. Browse
              available places and read their descriptions, locations,
              categories, and other information provided by the system.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-number">3</div>
            <h4>Choose Your Places</h4>
            <p>
              Select destinations based on your interests, such as
              history, spirituality, nature, wildlife, adventure,
              or cultural experiences.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-number">4</div>
            <h4>Plan Your Trip</h4>
            <p>
              Use the manual planner to organize your chosen places,
              or use the AI trip planner if available to generate
              a suggested itinerary based on your travel preferences.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-number">5</div>
            <h4>Review Your Journey</h4>
            <p>
              Review your planned destinations and itinerary.
              Where supported, check route directions, distances,
              estimated travel times, and other trip details.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-number">6</div>
            <h4>Travel with Safety Tools</h4>
            <p>
              Visit the Safety section to learn about available
              safety tools. If implemented, enable location monitoring
              with your consent, review geo-fence alerts, and use
              SOS incident reporting when needed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Feature explanations -->
    <section class="mb-5">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Understand Each Feature</h2>

      <p class="text-secondary mb-4">
        Learn what each module does and how it can help you.
      </p>

      <div class="row g-4">

        <div class="col-md-6">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">🏞️</div>
            <h4>1. Explore Maharashtra</h4>
            <p>
              Discover tourist attractions across different districts.
              Destination information helps you learn about a place
              before deciding whether to visit it.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Example:</strong> A traveller interested in
              history can explore Ajanta Caves, Ellora Caves, and
              Maharashtra's famous forts.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">🤖</div>
            <h4>2. AI Trip Planner</h4>
            <p>
              Enter your starting city, number of days, travel budget,
              interests, and preferred travel method. The system can
              use these preferences to suggest a suitable itinerary,
              when AI planning is available.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Example:</strong> A user planning a two-day
              historical trip can request a suggested schedule for
              visiting selected attractions.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">🗓️</div>
            <h4>3. Manual Trip Planner</h4>
            <p>
              Choose the destinations you want to visit and organize
              your trip according to your own preferences. This is
              useful when you already know where you want to go.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Example:</strong> Add Ellora Caves and
              Grishneshwar Temple to your travel plan.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">📍</div>
            <h4>4. Route and Location Assistance</h4>
            <p>
              Where integrated, map and GPS features help you identify
              your location and access directions between destinations.
              Travel-time and distance information can help you prepare
              your schedule.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Example:</strong> Check directions from your
              starting point to the first destination and then to
              your next planned stop.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">🛡️</div>
            <h4>5. Tourist Safety and Geo-Fencing</h4>
            <p>
              Geo-fencing uses a virtual boundary around a defined
              geographical area. With the necessary permissions and
              working GPS integration, the application can detect
              relevant boundary events and show configured alerts.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Example:</strong> If a configured restricted
              zone is entered, the system may display a warning
              according to its implemented rules.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">🚨</div>
            <h4>6. SOS and Incident Reporting</h4>
            <p>
              The incident reporting feature allows a user to submit
              information about a safety concern through the supported
              reporting workflow.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Example:</strong> A traveller can submit an
              incident report when they need to communicate a problem.
              An in-app report does not automatically mean emergency
              services have been contacted.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">💾</div>
            <h4>7. Saved Trips</h4>
            <p>
              Where enabled, save your planned itinerary and return
              to it later to review the destinations and travel
              schedule without preparing the same plan again.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Example:</strong> Save a weekend trip and open
              the saved plan when you are ready to review it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">⚙️</div>
            <h4>8. Admin Dashboard</h4>
            <p>
              Authorized administrators can manage destination
              information and maintain the tourism data displayed
              to users, according to their assigned permissions.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Example:</strong> An administrator can add
              a new tourist destination if the relevant management
              feature is available.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Example journey -->
    <section class="mb-5">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Example: A Tourist's Journey</h2>

      <div class="info-panel mt-3">
        <p>
          Imagine that a family wants to visit Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar
          for a weekend.
        </p>

        <ol class="mb-0">
          <li class="mb-2">
            They explore the available destinations on the platform.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-2">
            They choose places that match their interests.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-2">
            They use the manual planner or AI planner to organize
            their visit.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-2">
            They review the suggested itinerary and available
            directions before travelling.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-2">
            They review the Safety section and grant location
            permission only if they choose to use location-based
            functionality.
          </li>
          <li>
            They keep their itinerary available and enjoy exploring
            the region.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Privacy -->
    <section class="mb-5">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Your Privacy and Safety</h2>

      <div class="notice">
        <p class="mb-2">
          <strong>Your location should be used with your consent.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="mb-0">
          Location-based safety features may require GPS access and
          browser permission. Review the permission request before
          allowing access. GPS and browser permissions alone do not
          guarantee continuous monitoring, automatic emergency
          response, or contact with authorities. These capabilities
          depend on the application's implementation and available
          services.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Final CTA -->
    <section class="text-center py-4">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Ready to Explore Maharashtra?</h2>

      <p class="text-secondary">
        Discover new destinations, prepare your itinerary, and make
        your travel planning easier with the tools available on
        this platform.
      </p>

      <a href="/explore" class="btn btn-success btn-lg mt-3">
        Explore Destinations
      </a>
    </section>

  </main>